   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 80 of the laws of 2014, amending the vehicle and traffic law relating to the residential parking system in the village of Bronxville in the county of Westchester, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7871",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7871-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 80 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7871\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 80 of the laws of 2014,\namending the vehicle and traffic law relating to the residential\nparking system in the village of Bronxville in the county of\nWestchester, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo permit the Village of Bronxville to extend its local law allowing\nfor a residential parking permit system for a period of a year.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nChanges the expiration date of the law from January 1, 2017 to January\n1, 2018.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Village of Bronxville sought a law to allow a permit parking\nsystem for the period of significant construction displacing\nneighborhood residents. The construction is not finished and it is\nseeking an extension of the parking system for the period of a year.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATION :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the sixtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law and shall expire on January 1, 2018 when upon such the date\nthe provisions of the law shall be deemed repealed.\n",
